On Fri, Oct 18, 2013 at 8:29 AM, Pierre Abbat <phma@bezitopo.org> wrote:

> On Thursday, October 17, 2013 17:33:16 Michael Turniansky wrote:
> >   Using "pare" as the argument to "ju'u" is asking for trouble, since
> > interpreting its meaning depends upon the base you are in! Every
> numbering
> > system thinks it's in base "10".  That's why gai is a safer choice.
>
> "ju'u" being in VUhU makes no sense. It ought to be in PA3.
>
> What is "pa'i" for? It seems redundant to "fe'i".
>
>
    As redundant as parbi/frinu/dilcu  But for some reason, natlangs like
to treat ratios (a:b) distinct from fractions (a/b) and division (a=F7b).
 Perhaps because you can use ratios as n-ary operations, unlike fractions
or division.  Perhaps it's because we often leave ratios unevaluated *shrug=
*

      --gejyspa

